# netstat — real-world examples

> WARNING: netstat is deprecated — use `ss` and `ip` (see the table below).

## Which users/processes are listening on which ports

```sh
sudo netstat -lnptu
```

## View the routing table (-n disables DNS lookups)

```sh
netstat -r
```

## Which process is listening on a given port

```sh
netstat -pln | grep <port> | awk '{print $NF}'
# Example output: 1507/python
```

## Fast display of IPv4 TCP listening programs

```sh
sudo netstat -vtlnp --listening -4
```

## Modern replacements

```sh
sudo ss -tulpn          # instead of netstat -lnptu
ip route                # instead of netstat -r
ip -s link              # instead of netstat -i
ip maddr                # instead of netstat -g
```

## Homelab: is Plex listening on mediaserver?

```sh
sudo ss -tulpn | grep 32400
```

| Deprecated        | Replacement |
| ----------------- | ----------- |
| netstat -lnptu    | ss -tulpn   |
| netstat -r        | ip route    |
| netstat -i        | ip -s link  |
| netstat -g        | ip maddr    |
